# VS Code REST Client requests. Nothing secret lives in this file.
# Put your own values in .vscode/settings.json under "rest-client.environmentVariables"
# (that folder is git-ignored), for example:
#   { "local": { "token": "<jwt from sign-in>",
#                "adminPhone": "...", "adminPassword": "..." } }
# Then pick the "local" environment in the REST Client status bar.

@host = http://localhost:5000

### Sign up admin
post {{host}}/auth/sign-up/admin
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "full_name": "Demo Admin",
    "phone_number": "{{adminPhone}}",
    "password": "{{adminPassword}}",
    "language": "english",
    "admin_level": "admin"
}

### Sign in admin (copy the returned token into your "token" variable)
post {{host}}/auth/sign-in/admin
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "phone_number": "{{adminPhone}}",
    "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### List members
get {{host}}/admin/members
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create program
post {{host}}/admin/programs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "content": "https://example.com/program"
}

### List programs
get {{host}}/admin/programs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
